{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.sum_image_toList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.sum_image_toList","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L118-L125","doc":"**Sum transport (P5).** A sum of any `g : List ℕ → M` over the sorted-list model\n`Finset.univ.image toList` equals the abstract sum `∑_{Λ : Nat.Partition n} g (toList Λ)`.\nWith `g = (· ^ 2) ∘ dim` this identifies the Identity I model-side `∑ dim²` with the\n`Nat.Partition`-indexed Burnside sum of `RSKBridge`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_injective","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L114-L116","doc":"`toList` is injective: it is the bridge equivalence post-composed with `Subtype.val`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.equivSortedList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.equivSortedList","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L93-L103","doc":"**The bridge `Equiv`** — `Nat.Partition n ≃ {weakly-decreasing positive lists summing to n}`.\nThe right-hand subtype is precisely the computable model the Identity I combinatorics range over,\nso an abstract `∑_{Λ : Nat.Partition n}` transports to a sum over the sorted-list model and back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_ofList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_ofList","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**Round trip II** — `toList (ofList l …) = l` when `l` is already weakly decreasing.  Both\nsides are weakly-decreasing lists with the same underlying multiset, hence equal\n(`List.eq_of_perm_of_sorted`, using antisymmetry of `· ≥ ·` on `ℕ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList_toList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList_toList","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**Round trip I** — `ofList (toList p) … = p`.  Partitions are determined by their parts\nmultiset, and `toList` preserves it (`toList_coe`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList_parts","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L72-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.ofList","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L66-L70","doc":"Build a `Nat.Partition n` from any list of positive parts summing to `n` (order ignored). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_sum","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L61-L64","doc":"`toList p` sums to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Every entry of `toList p` is positive (a genuine partition has positive parts). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.mem_toList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.mem_toList","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L53-L55","doc":"Membership in `toList p` is membership in the parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_coe","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L49-L51","doc":"`toList p` carries exactly the parts multiset (sorting forgets nothing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L44-L47","doc":"`toList p` is weakly decreasing — the hypothesis the Identity I `(A)` proof consumes\n(`l.Sorted (· ≥ ·)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge.toList","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionListBridge.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The weakly-decreasing list of parts of a `Nat.Partition n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}